# XSH atomic_exchange(), atomic_exchange_explicit()
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.

assertion  XSH.atomic_exchange.001
anchor     functions/atomic_exchange.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/atomic_exchange.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      2024
says       atomic_exchange() stores the new value and returns the value held
           before, for atomic_bool and every atomic integer type, with the
           values 0, 1, the type's minimum and maximum.
test       t/001-exchange-values.c

assertion  XSH.atomic_exchange.002
anchor     functions/atomic_exchange.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      2024
says       atomic_exchange() on atomic pointer objects returns the pointer held
           before; in a chain of calls each returns what the previous call
           stored, also when the same value is stored again.
test       t/002-exchange-chain.c

assertion  XSH.atomic_exchange.003
anchor     functions/atomic_exchange.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/atomic_exchange.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      2024
says       atomic_exchange_explicit() stores the new value and returns the
           value held before with each of the six memory orders, for atomic
           _Bool and every atomic integer type.
test       t/003-exchange-explicit-orders.c

assertion  XSH.atomic_exchange.004
anchor     functions/atomic_exchange.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2024
says       Four threads exchanging 5000 unique tokens each into one atomic int
           (plain and acq_rel forms): every token and the initial 0 is
           returned to exactly one call or remains as the final value, so the
           exchanges are atomic read-modify-write operations.
test       t/004-exchange-contention.c
